-- W8 (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md, §4.2): where the "took its default"
-- event hangs when the rule that read the default does not run among the
-- main expression's own steps.
--
-- The event stays where the default was read: under the step that needed it,
-- inside the trace of that run, also when the run is late (the result is
-- written out after the main expression has finished). Only an event that the
-- trace has nowhere to show is put on the main expression: the last two
-- directives below.

IMPORT prelude

-- a definition with no inputs, which the trace does not unfold, decodes JSON
-- of its own: the field it leaves out takes its default inside it
DECLARE Config HAS
  timeout IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 30
  retries IS A NUMBER

GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH AN EITHER STRING Config
`parse config` s MEANS JSONDECODE s

GIVETH A NUMBER
`total budget` MEANS
  CONSIDER `parse config` "{\"retries\": 2}"
  WHEN RIGHT c THEN c's timeout PLUS c's retries
  WHEN LEFT e THEN 0

§ `Rates`
    GIVEN `the rate`     IS A NUMBER  TYPICALLY 3
          `has capacity` IS A BOOLEAN TYPICALLY TRUE

GIVETH A NUMBER
doubled MEANS IF `has capacity` THEN `the rate` TIMES 2 ELSE 0

GIVETH A NUMBER
tripled MEANS `the rate` TIMES 3

-- each of these runs `doubled` only when the answer is written out
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`maybe doubled` MEANS JUST doubled

GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`both as a list` MEANS LIST doubled, tripled

GIVETH A NUMBER
`add rate` n MEANS n PLUS `the rate`

GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`all plus the rate` MEANS map `add rate` (LIST 1, 2)

-- a record field nothing computes with: no run of a rule to hang it on
DECLARE Quote HAS rate IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A Quote
`quote at the rate` MEANS Quote `the rate`

-- two sections, each with an input of one name and a default of its own
§ `First`
    GIVEN `the span` IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 4

GIVETH A NUMBER
`first span` MEANS `the span`

§ `Second`
    GIVEN `the span` IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 9

GIVETH A NUMBER
`second span` MEANS `the span`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`both spans` MEANS `first span` PLUS `second span`

#EVALTRACE `maybe doubled`
#EVALTRACE `both as a list`
#EVALTRACE `all plus the rate`
#EVALTRACE `both spans`
#EVALTRACE `quote at the rate`
#EVALTRACE `total budget`
